      "description": "AHP pairwise comparisons of storefront component types (Table 3 of the paper): six categories (signage utilization, opening utilization, signage ratio, opening ratio, colour scheme, material palette), each shown as the paper's three-panel image of one storefront edited into three types; for every category three pairs (p1 = type 1 vs 2, p2 = 1 vs 3, p3 = 2 vs 3) on a 5-point scale: 1 = left type much more visible, 2 = left type more visible, 3 = equal, 4 = right type more visible, 5 = right type much more visible. One record per category, value {p1, p2, p3}, key = category id. Analysis as in the paper: convert to AHP judgements (e.g. 1→5, 2→3, 3→1, 4→1/3, 5→1/5), build a 3×3 matrix per respondent and category, derive type weights (principal eigenvector or geometric mean, aggregated across respondents) and check the consistency ratio (CR ≤ 0.1)."
